  "description": "Unleash the allure of the past with “Getting Blacker,” a font that encapsulates the distinctive style of the 80s and 90s. Perfectly suited for branding crafted beers and bold fashion. This font draws from the classical look of Blackletter Display, delivering a mix of gothic charm and dark academia aesthetic that evokes the spirit of death metal and underground rock. Expertly designed by Denustudio, “Getting Blacker” is not just a font – it’s a relic of old English charm that effortlessly blends into the modern age. It’s as sharp and edgy as a tattoo, wrapped within the class of Gothic Calligraphy, and replete with ornamental typography that reminds one of medieval times. This descriptor isn’t complete without a nod to its usage in merchandise and posters or the vintage touch it brings to Victorian themes. So whether you’re designing for a rock concert, a clothing brand, or a whiskey label, make sure to engrave your statement with the timeless elegance of “Getting Blacker”. So why hold off? It’s time to step up your design game and go medieval, go Gothic, go “Getting Blacker”.",
  "fullDescription": "<p>Unleash the allure of the past with “Getting Blacker,” a font that encapsulates the distinctive style of the 80s and 90s. Perfectly suited for branding crafted beers and bold fashion. This font draws from the classical look of Blackletter Display, delivering a mix of gothic charm and dark academia aesthetic that evokes the spirit of death metal and underground rock. Expertly designed by Denustudio, “Getting Blacker” is not just a font – it’s a relic of old English charm that effortlessly blends into the modern age. It’s as sharp and edgy as a tattoo, wrapped within the class of Gothic Calligraphy, and replete with ornamental typography that reminds one of medieval times. This descriptor isn’t complete without a nod to its usage in merchandise and posters or the vintage touch it brings to Victorian themes. So whether you’re designing for a rock concert, a clothing brand, or a whiskey label, make sure to engrave your statement with the timeless elegance of “Getting Blacker”. So why hold off? It’s time to step up your design game and go medieval, go Gothic, go “Getting Blacker”.</p>",
